!YSFlight - M1 test build
=========================

This is NOT the game yet. It is the YSFlight Community Edition console
server (no window, no graphics, no sound), built for RISC OS to check that
the simulator core works: loading the aircraft, maps and start positions,
and flying the AI traffic.

Needs: SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later and ARMEABISupport (PackMan).
PThreadTicker 0.03 is included and loaded by !Run.

Double-click !YSFlight. A task window opens and runs:
  1. the aircraft list        -> Logs.Aircraft (88 aircraft)
  2. the map list             -> Logs.Fields   (18 maps)
  3. Aomori start positions   -> Logs.Aomori   (36)
  4. Hawaii start positions   -> Logs.Hawaii   (56)
  5. the server, on the screen. It prints "Ready to go!" and then
     messages about AI aircraft taxiing and landing. Leave it a few
     minutes, then press Escape.
Each step's error output goes to a Logs file ending in E (AircraftE,
ServerE...). If the program crashes, that file has the RISC OS error
and a backtrace.

Settings are saved in <Choices$Write>.YSFlight.

Please report: the files in Logs, the task window's text (Save from its
menu), and any error box, with its exact text.

This is an unofficial port, not made or supported by the YSCE
developers. AI (Anthropic's Claude) has been used as a coding assistant.

